          <output>No changes there — matching the previous operation's boundary. The task is complete.

## Summary

`Task.run` on `A02_UpdatePageSkeletons` executed — operation #2 of the running transform `T00003_CreatePageSkeletons_20260912T025829`.

**1. Read the plan** — `BmlDocSetPlan.rootPageGroupPlan`: 25 `PagePlan` entries across 9 groups.

**2. Sources** — resolved `BlockMLSourceSet` (whitelist: `core/definition/documentation/type/…`). Found a strong prior draft (from the earlier, since-reset `T00002` run) and independently re-verified every bound source against the live `@blockml/core` model rather than trusting it:
- Confirmed the `is`/`documentation` text of ~30 `org.blockml.bml.documentation.*` Blocks actually supports each page's claims.
- Caught one stale binding: `org.blockml.bml.task.AuthorNewBlock` no longer exists — the package moved to `org.blockml.bml.documentation.howto.AuthorNewBlock`. Fixed `AuthorNewBlockGuide.bml` accordingly.
- Kept the one deliberate exception outside the whitelist: `TableOfContents` binds to `org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.Navigation`/`NavigationItem`, since no narrative source covers the navigation-menu topic and these structural Blocks are literally the SSOT for it.

**3–4. Wrote 25 skeletons** under `a02_structuring/data/page/docs/` — `dpage:DocPage` baseType, `is`/`documentation`/`purpose`/`detailLevel`/`pageType` set, bound sources listed as `Requires`/`SeeAlso`, no body aggregations.

**5. Registered on `BmlDocSet_A02`** — filled `pages` (25 entries, plan order) and `homePage` → `docs:TableOfContents`. `pageGroups` left empty (that's task #3's job). `Library.bml` already exported every `docs:*` page from before, so no catalog change was needed there.

**Validation** (`npx blockml validate --all`): only the pre-existing, out-of-scope `pagegroup:*` unknown-type errors remain (op #3's responsibility). No errors, no warnings on any file I touched — only the same `PREFER_MARKDOWN` style recommendations already present on sibling a03 pages. (I did hit and fix a self-inflicted issue along the way: a bulk `sed` cleanup of unused `dlevel:`/`ptype:` namespace warnings briefly corrupted `TableOfContents.bml`'s opening tag; caught it via validate and repaired it.)

**Changed files** (unstaged, no commit):
- `packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a02_structuring/data/BmlDocSet_A02.bml`
- `packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a02_structuring/data/page/` (25 new skeletons)

I left the running transform record (`_meta/transform/running/T00003_...bml`) and git state untouched, matching how operation #1 ended — flipping that operation to `Succeeded` and committing `transform(operation): T00003_CreatePageSkeletons_20260912T025829 #2` appears to be a separate step you haven't asked me to take.</output>
